<h1>Brave voyager, having made such an arduous journey from the rocky coasts of the orange website:</h1>
<article class="article-content rendered">

{% asMarkdown %}

By the earnest grace of peers and other readers sharing my work to wider oceans, I have now a handful of times faced the thrill and chill of front-paging on HN. By the general tone of the comments, it seems most of your peers do not come in peace. I try not fault you for it, but I’ve seen enough bad faith takes to last me a lifetime, and frankly I prefer to share my work with those who might get more value from it than reactivity; those who read my blog because they like it, or because their friends shared it.

_“Oh,”_ I hear you say, _“oh, well that’s not very open-minded.”_ _“If your posts are so good shouldn’t they stand infallibly up to scrutiny?”_, _“ah well, so much for the tolerant left”_ — friends, I have been online too long to still be falling for this kind of thing.

Ultimately I can’t and won’t stop anyone from diving any deeper, but to be frank: _most of you road-weary HN travelers are not going to like what you find here, and you’ll be better off at the next link on the list_. 

<a class="with-arrow with-arrow--out" href="#" onclick="history.back(); return false;">Kindly, gently, go back from whence thou camest.</a>

<a class="with-arrow" href="https://youtu.be/AtHeGZTMAo8">No, I insist. Show me that blasted post I came here for.</a>

{% endasMarkdown %}
</article>
